            <ArticleTitle>Node self-connections in network metrics.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1111/ele.12885</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Zamborain-Mason et al. (Ecol. Lett., 20, 2017, 815-831) state that they have newly proposed network metrics that account for node self-connections. Network metrics incorporating node self-connections, also referred to as intranode (intrapatch) connectivity, were however already proposed before and have been widely used in a variety of conservation planning applications.</AbstractText>
